      "message": "feat(post): probe positioning moves post as protected stop-on-contact moves\n\nThe descent from the rapid / safe plane to each touch's start, the bore\nentry and the rise of a probe cycle were plain G01 feeds: a part or\nclamp not where the model says broke the stylus on them. The dump now\nmarks every non-rapid move of a probe path that is not a touch or its\nback-off as a GUARD record (Record::Guard, docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md),\nand the engine calls the new onProbeGuard hook for it:\n\n- Fanuc: G31 to the point, then per moving axis\n  IF[ABS[#506n-end]GT0.001]THEN#3000=3(PROBE HIT ON POSITIONING) - the\n  skip position equals the block end only when no contact came.\n- Tormach PathPilot: G38.3 to the point, then o5001 if [#5070 EQ 1] /\n  (MSG, PROBE HIT ON POSITIONING) / M2 / o5001 endif (LinuxCNC G-code\n  reference: G38.3, #5070, O-codes).\n\nA post script without onProbeGuard is refused by name, once per\noperation. An inverted axis mirrors a GUARD like an absolute move.\nPinned by probe_guard (marking, stream round-trip, Fanuc corner golden,\nTormach guard golden, refusal) and the regenerated Fanuc probe goldens.\n\nFixes #174\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
